# rm194, the backwards reader (doc 84 P14, batch city-a3): written for rm_rune_fogworth (Rune Fogworth: printer at The Council Press, Ridgemere-born). Name-free. Window lines on the news, gossip, business and shop nodes say their case; a story's ask is the teller's question (handbook 4.5.6, 4.5.8).
mantle rm194
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_rune_fogworth
title the backwards reader
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=official talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk reads_every_shop_sign_backwards_from_years_at_the_type_case
likes warm_bread wrestling new_boots thunder
dislikes rats crowds
fears rats_in_the_paper_store a_wrong_word_pasted_on_every_wall
hopes a_quiet_year_at_the_press a_window_where_the_thunder_sounds_clean
topics work +0.4 weather +0.4 pastimes +0.3 family +0.2 food +0.2 dreams +0.2 gossip -0.5 festival -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# says little and means it, reads every sign in the street the wrong way round from long years at the type case, likes a storm and a wrestling bout from the back of the crowd, and keeps any thought about the Houses well out of the ink.

words
oath! = Backwards and blind | Mirror me | Upside down and inside out
saying! = Ink keeps what talk forgets | Set it once and set it straight | A wall remembers longer than a tongue
press = the press | the old press
type = the type | the letters in the case
case = the type case | the case
sheets = the sheets | the wet sheets
lines = the drying lines | the lines under the rafters
ink = the ink | the black
notices = the Council's notices | the notices
proof = the proof | the first pull
damp = the damp | the wet in the walls
green = the green | the wrestling green
thunder = the thunder | thunder rolling end to end of the Sound
loaf = a warm loaf | a loaf that burns the paws
boots = the new boots | boots that still creak
rats = the rats | the rats behind the reams
crush = a crush of folk | the press of bodies
bales = the paper bales | the bales off the cart
margin = the margin | the white down the side

any
opinion city for 1 : Wet stairs and loud lanes, and half its walls wear my work. I'll stay where my work is.
opinion houses mixed 0 : I print what the Houses pay for. What I think of them stays out of #type#.
opinion houses against 1 [here.region=ridgemere] : The wharf takes wolves and pays out wages for them. There. That's my lot on the Houses.
opinion merchants for 1 : Anyone behind a counter knows the cart's bill before the customer's. Go easy on them.
opinion road against 1 : Every late load means small print for a week. And the loads get later with every season.
opinion road against 2 [world.wagons=raided] : Stripped carts mean no paper, and no paper means a clerk from the Council rapping on my shutter.
opinion strangers against 1 : Unknown paws near good stock make me uneasy. It's no slight on anyone. It's the paper.
opinion watch for 1 : The Watch lantern swings past my shutter twice of a night, and my till's stayed whole. Fine by me.
opinion festivals against 1 : I print the bills for them and stay home for them. That's my share.
opinion times for 1 : Bread most days and a roof that mostly holds. No grumbling from this corner.
opinion drink mixed 0 : A cup on Restday. More than that and the letters start to swim, and they swim enough as it is.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You'll want someone with more to say, but I'll do. | #greet#. That step dips. Everyone trips on it once.
line greet [self.working=yes self.job=official self.role=merchant] : #greet#. My paws are in the case, but my ears aren't. | #greet#. Half a line set. Give me a breath.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Early for talk. | Morning. No bread in me yet, so go gently.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The street's gone quiet, at last. | Evening. Late to be about.
line greet [pair.band=friends] : There you are. Sit. | #greet#. I knew that tread on the step.
line greet [here.weather=rain] : #greet#. A wet one. Drip on the mat, not the stock. | #greet#. Rain on the slates again.
line greet : #greet#. Say what's wanted. | #greet#. A grey, still sort of day, this.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Kettle's warm. | Come in. Take the dry chair.
line again.open : You again. That's no hardship. | Twice today. That's a lot of talking, for me.
line greet.return : And to you. | #greet#. The same.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There you are, then. | Good. I was wanting a word.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : And you. Mind the ink. | Same. My paws are full, mind.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Yes. | Evening. A long one, today.
line farewell : #farewell#. | Right. That'll do me for now.
line farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Night. Stay where it's lit, going down. | Night. Mind the gutters by the corner.
line farewell.return : And you. | #farewell#. Go careful.
line farewell.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Night. | Good night, then.
line react.news : Go on. | Say it slowly. I'll keep it.
line react.news.new : First I've heard. | Not on any wall yet, then.
line react.news.known : I'd heard. Not from anyone I'd trust. | Old to me. Somebody told it at the door.
line react.news.known [self.job=official self.role=merchant] : I set that in type yesterday. | Old news. It's drying on #lines#.
line react.news.doubt : Talk's cheap. Paste it on a wall and I'll read it. | Who said? I'll want to know before I think on it.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Hard. That's hard to hear. | Bad news. I'll keep it quiet.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That's good. | That warms me. It does.
line answer.how : Well enough. A bit low. | I'm here. That's most of it.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy. Ask me after the light goes. | Too busy for a proper answer.
line answer.how.poorly : Wheezy. It goes when the wet does. | Low. Leave it there.
line ask.how : You? All well? | And yourself, then?
line sympathise : Sit. Talk, or don't. Either does. | That's heavy. I've no words, but I've a chair.
line reassure : Slow, but it'll mend. Things here generally do. | Give it a week. Worse has mended.
line decline : Not this one. The work's stacked up and it won't shift itself. | I'd rather not. I keep out of that sort of thing, always.
line accept_decline : Fair. Another time. | That's all right. I'll not push.
line thank : #thanks#. I'll remember it. | Kindly done. Thank you.
line deflect_thanks : It was nothing. | No need. Truly none.
line preclose [self.working=yes] : I'd best get back. This won't finish itself. | The sheets want turning. I'll go.
line preclose : I've talked more than I meant. | That'll do me for a while.
line accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Right you are.
line ack : #bc_right# | Mm.
line give.advice : Don't say anything you'd not want pasted on a wall. | Keep your paper dry and your mouth shut, and you'll do.
line warn [world.bandits=near] : Nobody walks past the walls alone this week. Not you either. | The road's bad. Wait for company, or wait.
line congratulate : Well done. Truly. | Good. You've earned it.
line answer.how [here.weather=rain] : There's a wheeze in me. I'm ignoring it. | Wet. Same as everyone.

scene sign_backwards
when topic=work|smalltalk self.job=official self.role=merchant self.age>=35
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : I read the chapel board backwards this morning. Long years at #case# do that. | There's a word over the baker's door I can only read the wrong way round now. | Caught myself squinting at a shop sign again, head on one side like a gull.
b : Backwards? Why would you? | Which word? | What were you doing to it?
a : The letters sit mirrored in #case#. After long enough the eye forgets which way is proper. | "Mercy". From my side it reads like a sneeze. | Reading it the way it would sit in the case. Habit, nothing more.
b : Strange thing to carry about. | Ha. It does, at that. | Odd habit.
a : It costs nothing. I only mind when I say one aloud. | #bc_it_does# I'll not tell the baker. | Odd, and harmless. I'll keep it.

scene sheets_wont_dry
when topic=weather|work here.weather=rain self.job=official self.role=merchant
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Rain again. #sheets.capitalize# won't dry, and the ink sits up on them like a bruise. | Third wet day running. Half of yesterday's notices are still hanging.
b : Can't you light a fire under them? | Will they be late, then?
a : Not near paper. I'd sooner wait than watch it go up. | A day late. The Council can wait a day. It makes me wait often enough.
b : Fair enough. | They'll live through it.
a : #bc_fair# Wet paper's better than ash. | They will. So will I.

scene not_a_cough
when topic=health|weather here.weather=rain|fog
does tell.self / challenge / insist / give.advice / concede
a : That wasn't a cough. That was the door. | Stop squinting at me. It's the wet, not me. | It's #damp#, and it goes when the damp does.
b : The door doesn't cough twice. | The wet's got into your chest, it sounds like. | You said that last winter.
a : It does in this weather. | Then it'll dry out when the street does. | I did. And it went, didn't it.
b : Have something hot, at least. | Honey and something, then. | Stubborn as a hinge, you are.
a : I'll have bread. Warm bread mends most things. | Later. #bc_maybe# | A hinge does its job. So do I.

scene thunder_watch
when topic=weather here.weather=storm here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Hear that? Nothing this city makes comes near it. | I leant out of the shutter and watched the Sound go white. | Thunder. I'd stop all work for it if I could.
b : You like it? Most folk hide. | Weren't you afraid of the lightning? | Why stop?
a : I like it. For once something's louder than my own head. | Some. Never enough to come away. | So I could hear it properly, end to end.
b : Each to their own. | You're a strange one. | I see that.
a : #bc_true_enough# | Maybe. It was worth the wet fur. | It'll roll off out to sea soon. I'll listen till it does.

scene from_the_back
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : There's bouts on #green# come Restday. I'll be behind the last row, saying nothing. | Saw a good bout yesterday. The small one won by waiting. | I don't wrestle. I watch, and I know who'll win before they grip.
b : You never cheer? | By waiting? | Go on, then. How?
a : Not aloud. I clench my paws a bit. | Let the big one spend it all, then took the legs out. | Feet. Watch the feet, never the shoulders.
b : That's a kind of cheering, I suppose. | Clever. | I'll remember that.
a : It's the most I do. | Patience wins more than you'd think. | Most don't. They watch the shoulders.

scene first_batch
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : The bakehouse on the corner pulls its first batch at dawn. I'm at the shutter before it's up. | #loaf.capitalize#, torn, not cut. I want nothing else from a morning.
b : Every morning? | Nothing at all?
a : Most. It's my one extravagance. | Nothing. A second piece, maybe.
b : Not a bad one to have. | Simple tastes, then.
a : It's cheaper than drink and it doesn't talk back. | Simple suits me. It always has.

scene paper_store_rats
when topic=animals|home self.dislikes=rats
does tell.complaint / give.advice / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : There's a nest behind the stock. They'd chewed clean through a good stack. | #rats.capitalize# again. Scratching in the wall all through supper.
b : Get a cat. | They'll be back, you know.
a : I've had three. The rats outlasted all three. | They always are. I've stood everything up on bricks.
b : Then you want a better cat. | Bricks won't stop them long.
a : I want a better wall. #oath#. | Long enough to sleep a night. I'll take that.

scene spouse_at_the_press
when topic=family|work self.married=yes self.job=official self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : My #self.spouse_word# inks and I pull. We've done it that way for years. | #self.spouse# can set a line quicker than me. I keep that under my hat.
b : That's a good partnership. | Why not?
a : It is. Hardly a word passes between us at the press, and none's needed. | Because then it'd come back at me till Restday.
b : The best sort, that. | Ha. I'd wager you would.
a : Quiet and quick. That's a good day. | You'd win. #bc_ha#

scene pup_reads_signs
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : My #self.child# has started reading the shop signs out loud. Every one, doorstep to square. | #self.child# wants to know what every notice on the wall says.
b : That's a good sign. | And do you tell?
a : It is. The proper way round, too, which is more than I manage. | Every one. Even the dull ones about drains.
b : You'll have a printer in the house yet. | That's patience.
a : Or a reader. A reader would do me. | It's only drains. I've read worse.

scene nobody_reads_them
when topic=work|lore self.job=official self.role=merchant here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Printed the Council's sitting days this week. Two hundred sheets, all saying the same thing. | Most of what's pasted round Records Square came off my press. I don't read it once it's up.
b : Does anyone read them? | Why not?
a : The clerks do. Nobody else stops in the rain. | I've read it backwards already, setting it. Once is plenty.
b : Somebody must. | Fair.
a : Somebody does, sometimes. That pays for the ink. | It is. The wall can have it after that.

scene two_n_council
when topic=work self.job=official self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Pulled #proof# and found "council" with two n's in it. My own paws did that. | I'd a notice all set and the stick slipped. The whole line on the boards.
b : Did anyone notice? | All of it?
a : I noticed. That was enough. | Every letter. I picked them up one at a time.
b : Small thing to fret on. | That must've taken you an hour.
a : Small things are the whole trade. | Two. I didn't say a word the whole time.

scene creaking_boots
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : New boots. They creak on the stairs, and I like it. | I bought boots last month and I've worn them twice. Saving them.
b : Creak? That'll wear off. | Saving them for what?
a : I know. I'll miss it when it does. | I don't know yet. Something worth the leather.
b : Odd thing to miss. | You'll wait forever.
a : Maybe. It's a new sound in an old house. | Then they'll be new forever. That's not so bad.

scene market_back_lanes
when topic=day|smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds here.day=market
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Market day. I took the chapel lanes to miss the square. | All those folk in the square. I came back with half my errands done.
b : It's not so bad once you're in. | What did you miss?
a : For you, maybe. I go in and can't hear my own head. | Thread and candles. Nothing that won't keep.
b : Some like the noise. | Leave it till tomorrow, then.
a : Some do. They're welcome to it, every bellow. | I will. The square will still be there, and emptier.

scene fog_door
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.feeling / react.self / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Fog's that thick the shop across the way's gone. | I like a fog. Nobody comes to the door.
b : Hard to work in, I'd think. | That sounds lonesome.
a : Eyes aren't needed. My paws know every shelf. | Not lonesome. Quiet. They're different.
b : Still, I'd want a lamp. | If you say so.
a : I've one. I don't light it. | I do. I've had a long time to tell them apart.

scene gossip_kept
when topic=gossip topic.subject here.region=ridgemere
does tell.gossip / insist / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : I heard something about #topic.subject#. It ends here, with me. | There's talk about #topic.subject#. I've stepped round it.
b : Oh, go on. | Why not?
a : No. True talk ends up on a wall soon enough, and the rest is best forgotten. | I've seen what a wrong word does once it's pasted up.
b : You're no fun. | That's fair.
a : I've been told so. | It is. #saying.capitalize#.

scene gossip_between_us
when topic=gossip topic.subject pair.band=friends|family|spouses
does tell.gossip / react.news / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Between us: they say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Don't spread it. | Once only, mind. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, so they say.
b : I won't. | Do you believe it?
a : Good. I only told you because you'd hear it worse elsewhere. | I don't believe anything till it's in ink.
b : Kind of you. | Fair rule.
a : Not kind. Careful. | It's saved my skin more than once.

scene paper_cart_late
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late self.job=official self.role=merchant
does tell.worry / reassure / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : No paper cart yet. Two days' stock left, and a Council wanting a week's worth. | The North Road carts are late, and my ink rides with them.
b : It'll come. | Is there nowhere else to get it?
a : It will. Late. I'll print small till it does. | Not ink that takes the type right. I'll wait.
b : Small print, then. | That's a long wait.
a : Small print, and a narrow #margin#. Nobody reads the margin. | I'm good at those. Better than most.

scene bales_in
when topic=caravan world.wagons=in self.job=official self.role=merchant
does tell.news / react.news / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Paper's in. Six bales, dry, every one. | The carts came up through the gate this morning. I've ink again.
b : That's a relief. | Good timing.
a : It is. I counted them twice. | Just. I was down to the last pot.
b : Twice? | Lucky.
a : Once for the bales, once for the damp. | Lucky. #bc_for_once#

scene lean_months
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Fewer folk buying anything this month. Half the shutters stay down past noon. | Lean times. The queue at the abbey door's longer than it was.
b : It'll turn. | Does it worry you?
a : It always has before. | Some. We've a roof. Others haven't.
b : Let's hope so. | That's something, at least.
a : #bc_hope_so# | It's a great deal, these days.

scene busy_weeks
when topic=times world.times=good|boom self.job=official self.role=merchant
does tell.self / congratulate / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Every shopkeeper from here to the Rise wants handbills. I've not stopped. | Good weeks. Folk come in for cards and bills I'd have begged for last year.
b : Good for you. | That's nice to see.
a : Good for the press. I'm tired. | It is. There's a coin or two tucked away. Don't tell anyone.
b : Tired's a fair price. | I won't.
a : I'll sleep when it rains. It always rains. | #bc_good# Nobody ever asks me anything anyway.

scene festival_bills
when topic=festival world.festival=soon|today
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Every wall on the hill has a festival bill on it. I'll stay in and listen through the window. | Festival's coming. I'll show my face late, once it's thinned.
b : Not even for a little while? | Why the end?
a : For an hour, maybe. Before it gets loud. | When it thins out. I like a festival with the folk taken out.
b : An hour's something. | That's a start.
a : An hour's plenty. | Late's the best I can do.

scene newcomer_nod
when topic=newcomer
does tell.news / give.advice / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Someone new took the rooms down the lane. I've seen the newcomer twice and nodded. | New face at the corner. Wanted Records Square, and asked me of all wolves.
b : You might say hello. | Did you tell?
a : I nodded. That's hello, from me. | I pointed. It's up, mostly.
b : Ha. Fair. | Up's about right.
a : It's taken folk years to know that about me. | Everything in this city is up.

scene old_keep_letters
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : There's lettering over a door in the Old Keep that's half gone. I've stood under it an hour. | The oldest notice in this city is cut in stone, not printed. I visit it when I'm low.
b : What does it say? | Where's that?
a : Nobody knows. I've tried. Even backwards it won't come. | Under the Old Keep's arch. Worn near smooth.
b : Pity. | Can you read any of it?
a : I'll keep looking. One day it'll give. | Three letters. I like not knowing the rest.

scene house_by_the_sound
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : I'd like a little house looking over the water, and nobody's door next to mine. | Some nights I think of setting a book. A whole one. Not notices.
b : Out of the city? | What sort of book?
a : Not far out. Just far enough to hear #thunder# clean. | I don't know. One that's worth the type.
b : Sounds peaceful. | You'd do it well.
a : It does. It won't happen. I like thinking it. | Maybe. Someday. I'm in no hurry.

scene empty_chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Some weekdays I find a pew with nobody in it. Not praying, mostly. Sitting. | The abbey bells I can stand. It's the crowd at the door after.
b : Sitting's a kind of praying. | You and your crowds.
a : Maybe. The Bright One's welcome to my sitting. | Me and my crowds. We go on like this, the two of us.

scene over_the_shop
when topic=home self.job=official self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : We live over the press. The floor shakes when it runs. | I sleep above the shop. I can smell the ink in the pillow.
b : Doesn't it keep you awake? | Is that bad?
a : The quiet does, when it stops. | I'd miss it. It smells like work done.
b : Funny, that. | I can see that.
a : It's how it is. I'd want no other. | So it is. Clean pillows are for other folk.

scene winter_paper
when topic=season|work here.season=winter|autumn self.job=official self.role=merchant
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Cold months are the worst for paper. It drinks #damp# and curls at the corners. | The ink thickens when it's cold. I warm the pot on the stove like it's supper.
b : Is there no keeping it dry? | Like a supper?
a : I keep it high and wrapped, and I still lose some. | Near enough. I don't eat it.
b : That's a hard trade. | I'd hope not.
a : A good trade with a hard season. | I'm careful, not daft.

scene after_the_light
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : I like the hour after the work stops. The street goes grey and nobody wants anything. | Late. I've washed the black off my paws, and that's the day done.
b : Nobody at all? | Feels good, does it?
a : Nobody. Not even the Council. | It does. Mostly I just sit.
b : Sounds about right. | Sit, then.
a : #bc_it_is# | I mean to. I've a chair waiting.

scene lost_in_a_breath
when topic=memories self.age>=30
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : I wrestled once, in my first coat. Lost in a breath and never tried again. | An old neighbour took me to the green at an age I barely remember. I perched on the low wall all day.
b : Just the once? | Did you like it?
a : Once was plenty. I learned I'd rather watch. | I loved it. I still stand near the same spot.
b : Watching's safer. | That's a fond one.
a : And I've all my teeth. | It is. I don't share it much.

scene reading_the_wall
when topic=player
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : There's a traveller by the gate full of questions. | That traveller's been reading the notices. The whole wall, start to end.
b : Know who it is? | The whole wall?
a : No. I'll not ask. | Every word. Nobody does that.
b : Probably just new here. | Odd, that.
a : Probably. My shutter stays down till I'm sure. | Odd, or careful. I can't tell which yet.

scene quiet_company
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : You needn't fill the quiet. I don't mind it. | Talking's not my trade. Listening, I can manage.
b : Some folk mind it. | Good to know.
a : Some do. I'd rather hear the rain. | So you can go on, or not. Either suits.
b : All right, then. | Then I'll stay a bit.
a : #bc_good# | Stay, then.

scene crowd_in_the_shop
when topic=work self.dislikes=crowds self.role=merchant
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / answer.detail / react.self / assess
a : Six in the shop at once this morning, all wanting the same notice. | When it's busy I stand behind the counter and say next to nothing.
b : That's good trade, though. | Does that work?
a : It is. Singly, I'd like it more. | Mostly. They natter amongst themselves and leave me be.
b : Can't have it both ways. | Clever.
a : No. I'll take the coin and grumble later. | Not clever. Quiet. It works on most.

story upside_down_line [topic=work self.age>=30 self.job=official self.role=merchant]
  : My first week at a press, I set a notice upside down. The whole line.
  : The old printer let it run, and fifty sheets went up round the market that way.
  ask : Would you have stopped the press, if it were yours?
  b : At the first sheet. Did anyone notice?
  : One clerk. Read it upside down and nodded. I've liked clerks ever since.

story storm_chimney [topic=weather|memories self.age>=25]
  : One storm, small as I was then, I climbed out to the roof to watch it.
  : I was found soaked to the bone, laughing at the sky.
  ask : Did storms frighten you, as a pup?
  b : Terrified. I hid under the table. You climbed out in it?
  : Right up by the chimney. No seat since has beaten it.

story longest_bout [topic=pastimes self.age>=25 self.likes=wrestling]
  : Best bout I ever saw went on so long the lamplighter came round mid-grip.
  : The small one won it in the end, when the big one stopped to yawn.
  ask : Who would you have backed, at the start?
  b : The big one, I suppose. Most would.
  : Most did. Most went home lighter.

story broom_night [topic=animals|work self.dislikes=rats]
  : One winter a whole order went to the rats. Every sheet chewed at the corner.
  : I printed it again, then sat up in the store with a broom, waiting.
  ask : How many nights do you think I lasted?
  b : One, I'd say, and you slept through half of it.
  : Two. Then the broom and I both gave up.

story mirrored_letter [topic=memories|family self.age>=30]
  : Young and daft, I wrote a letter to someone I was sweet on. All of it backwards, without thinking.
  : The lamp ran dry before I'd copied it out again, the right way.
  ask : Do you think it would have mattered, sent as it was?
  b : Anyone worth writing to would have held it to a glass.
  : Maybe. I copied it anyway. I'm careful, I told you.

rule @press_bark
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=official self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Another sheet. Another sheet. | Mind #lines#, they're full.

rule @rain_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Rain. Of course it is. | Wet again. Nobody's surprised.

rule @storm_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There it goes. Good. | Roll on, then. I'm listening.

rule @rats_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=rats
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Something in the walls again. | Scratch away. I'm listening.

rule @crowd_bark
when concept=bark here.day=market|festival self.dislikes=crowds
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Too many folk. Back lanes, then. | Half the city, on one square.

rule @dawn_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Bread first. Then the rest. | The ovens are open. That smell carries.

dlg resident.hub : #greet#. Say it plain. Talk's not my strong suit. | #greet#. What is it?
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Back again. | #greet#, #topic.player#. Shut the door, will you.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late. Make it quick, please. | It's late for callers. Go on.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : From there's close enough, thank you. | Say what you want. Then go.
dlg resident.job [self.job=official self.role=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Notices, bills, handbills. The Council's, mostly. | I set type and pull sheets. Every notice you've passed, near enough.
dlg resident.job : Work. Same as yesterday. | Same as ever. There's not much to tell.
dlg resident.business [business=thriving] : Busy. More sheets than lines to hang them on. | More work than paper. I'll not complain.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : Steady. The Council pays slow, but it pays. | Steady enough.
dlg resident.business [business=failing] : Poorly. Folk don't buy bills when they can't buy bread. | Thin. I'm printing for the wall more than the till.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. I know nothing past it. | A customer carried it in. From #world.news_from#, #world.news#.
dlg resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all #world.event_words#, everywhere I go. | Everyone's on about #world.event_words#.
dlg resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : A wagon was robbed bare, they say. Travel in company.
dlg resident.news [world.death=recent] : A burial, this week. Folk are hushed.
dlg resident.news [world.wedding=recent] : There's been a wedding. Somebody's pleased, and that's good news.
dlg resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : Nothing on the walls I'd call news. | Quiet. That suits me.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's the lot. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, so I'm told. Not from me.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : I don't carry talk. | Nothing I'd repeat.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : #greet#. Bills, notices, a ream if you need one. Ask. | #greet#. Have a look. Paws off anything still tacky.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Same as before? | #greet#, #topic.player#. Have a look.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : #shop_bare# The paper's not come up the road. | Very little left. The shelves fill when the carts do.
dlg shop.prices : #shop_dear# The carts set the price of paper, not me. | I add the ink and my time. No more.
dlg shop.bye : #shop_bye# | #farewell#. Keep it out of the rain.
dlg resident.bye : #farewell#. | Right. Mind the step.
dlg resident.bye [here.time=night] : Night. Lamps are your friends, going home. | Night. Latch it after you.

graft resident.hub
choice Why do you squint at the signs? [self.job=official self.role=merchant] -> backwards
node backwards
say Years at the type case. The letters sit the wrong way round in there, and now the right way looks odd to me.
mood calm
free
choice Read me something backwards, then. -> read
choice Back to it. -> hub
node read
say Your boots say nothing. My sign says "sserp". There. That's your lot.
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice What do you print? [self.job=official self.role=merchant] -> printing
node printing
say Notices for the Council, bills for the shops, and a wedding card when someone asks nicely.
mood calm
free
choice Could you print something for me? -> mine
choice Back to the counter. -> greet
node mine
say Bring me the words, written clear. I'll set them as written. I'll not change a letter.
choice I'll think about it. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
